# simpleisadvanced.com public site

## Purpose

This is the deployed GitHub Pages site for Simple is Advanced. The current
publication is `The Alignment-Industrial Complex`. Its public reader offers
about two and a half opening paragraphs of every chapter and supporting
section, bounded at 180 body words. The contents page is the main entry point;
normal pages and the optional speed reader use the same excerpt selection.
Every preview invites readers to acquire the complete book. Earlier books have transition
pages at their existing URLs; the homepage does not currently promote them.

## Repository structure

```text
site/
  index.html                         homepage, hand-edited
  robots.txt                         crawler directives, hand-edited
  sitemap.xml                        assembled from section fragments
  og-image.png                       homepage social image
  articles/                          published essays and their feed
  alignment-industrial-complex/      generated by book4
  the-end-of-alignment/              legacy transition
  illusions-of-work/                 retired-book transition
  illusions-in-the-boardroom/        retired-book transition
  scripts/assemble_sitemap.py        sitemap authority
  tests/test_seo.py                  local and production verification
```

## Reader and search model

Static chapter pages provide normal reading, sequential navigation,
accessibility, structured data and search entry points. The RSVP reader is an
alternative way to read the same short previews. Both paths stop after each
excerpt and invite readers to continue with the complete edition.
`contents.html` links every chapter preview. Public HTML and JSON must contain
only the selected opening excerpt, never the remainder of any chapter. The generated reader data directories are blocked in
`robots.txt` because raw word arrays are not web pages.

## Ownership

Hand-edited in this repository:

- `index.html`
- `robots.txt`
- `404.html`
- `og-image.png`
- article pages and article indexes

Generated in a book repository and copied here by its publication target:

- every file under a book slug;
- each book's `sitemap-fragment.xml`; and
- the assembled `sitemap.xml` and `scripts/sitemap-state.json` after publish.

Do not hand-edit generated book directories. Change their source repository,
rebuild, and republish.

## Verification

```sh
python3 tests/test_seo.py
python3 tests/test_seo.py --live
```

The local gate checks metadata, structured data, article coverage, sitemap
completeness, crawler rules, social assets and filesystem resolution. Run the
live gate after every deployment.

## Retirement rule

Do not delete an earlier book or article merely because its material was
absorbed into the current book. Preserve incoming links with a mapped
transition page or an HTTP redirect at the hosting layer, remove the retired
page from the sitemap, add `noindex`, and point its canonical URL to the exact
replacement. Delete the old content only after the redirect path is operating
and search migration has been observed.
